"Software" means the GEL RAM source code, documentation, build material and other files to which a release expressly applies this license, excluding Third-Party Material.

"Third-Party Material" means separately identified material supplied under independent license terms, not portions of a Modification required to be licensed under section 6. Third-Party Material remains subject to its own license terms and is not relicensed by this license. Another person's authorship of a GEL RAM-derived Modification does not by itself make that Modification exempt Third-Party Material.

"Modification Author" means a person or entity that owns or is authorized to license copyright or patent rights in portions it adds to a Modification. A Modification Author does not thereby become the Project Licensor or acquire authority over another person's rights.

"Modification" means any change to, adaptation of, derivative work based on, or work containing modified portions of the Software.

"User Content" means independently supplied or created conversations, notes, documents, images, audio, video, personal knowledge, ORB payloads, and other input or output data that do not incorporate the Software or a Modification. Merely processing, encoding, quantizing, storing, or retrieving User Content with the Software does not make it a Modification. Code or executable instructions incorporating the Software or a Modification do not become User Content merely because they are encoded in an ORB or another data container.

"Corresponding Source" means the preferred form for making changes to a Modification, including all source code, interface definitions, build scripts, dependency manifests, configuration required to build and run the Modification, and scripts or source inputs necessary to reproduce generated source that forms part of the Modification. Corresponding Source does not require disclosure of passwords, private keys, personal data, unrelated datasets, or third-party material that the recipient is not legally permitted to redistribute, provided those exclusions are not used to conceal source necessary to understand, build, modify, or run the Modification.

For separately licensed, unmodified external dependencies, Corresponding Source may identify their exact versions, applicable licenses and lawful acquisition and build instructions instead of redistributing them, to the extent their own licenses permit. This exception does not excuse withholding GEL RAM-derived source. If necessary rights or required source cannot lawfully be supplied, this license does not authorize distributing or providing that Modification in violation of those requirements.

"Public Source Location" means an Internet location from which any person can obtain the complete Corresponding Source without payment, invitation, discriminatory access restriction, or proprietary client software beyond an ordinary web browser or generally available version-control client.

"Commercial Purpose" means use by or for You or Your Group that directly or indirectly supports, enables, improves, protects, markets, sells, delivers, or reduces the cost of a commercial activity or a profit-seeking organization. It includes, without limitation: use in or for a paid product or service; SaaS or hosted services; advertising-supported services; paid consulting; contract work; internal business operations; production infrastructure; customer support; commercial research and development; model, data, or system development intended for commercial deployment; and use that creates measurable operational, competitive, or economic advantage for a for-profit entity.

"Noncommercial Purpose" means a purpose that is not a Commercial Purpose. Personal study, hobby use, independent noncommercial research, education, charitable activity, and public-interest research are Noncommercial Purposes only when they are not performed for, funded primarily for the benefit of, or intended to deliver a commercial advantage to a for-profit entity.

An individual's employment by, or affiliation with, a for-profit entity does not by itself make that individual's separate personal activity a Commercial Purpose. Activity performed for that entity or its business benefit remains subject to the Commercial Purpose definition.

"Evaluation" means temporary internal examination of an unmodified copy of the Software solely to decide whether to seek a commercial license. Evaluation does not include production use, customer-facing use, deployment into business operations, training or tuning a production system, generation of commercial research output, or use to obtain operational, competitive, or economic advantage.

Internal test measurements used solely for that licensing decision are permitted Evaluation, not permission to use the Software or its outputs in the business activities excluded above.

