5. Reciprocity for Modifications

You may create, run, study, and retain a Modification solely for Your own Noncommercial Purposes privately without a time limit, provided You do not distribute it, provide another person access to it, or use it to provide functionality to another person. Such private use alone does not require publication of Corresponding Source. It does not authorize a Commercial Purpose.

If You distribute a Modification, provide another person access to it, or use it to provide functionality to another person, You must make its complete Corresponding Source available at a Public Source Location under this same license no later than the first such distribution, access, or provision of functionality. This includes functionality supplied through a network, a hosted service, or a peer-to-peer node, whether access is public, invitation-only, or limited to friends. An intermediary or wrapper does not remove this obligation when You supply functionality of a Modification through it.

For a Modification whose publication obligation has been triggered, the Public Source Location must remain available throughout its distribution or availability or provision of functionality to another person, and for at least three years after Your last such act. Subsequent solely private use does not extend that period. Later versions distributed or made available in these ways must have their corresponding source available on the same terms.

You must provide a prominent source notice identifying the Public Source Location in the Modification's documentation and, where reasonably practical, in the user-facing interface or command-line help.

This section does not require You to submit a pull request, transfer ownership of Your changes to the Licensor, or sign a contributor agreement merely to use or publish a Modification. Acceptance of an upstream contribution is a separate process.

User Content is not Corresponding Source and need not be published under this section. This license grants no rights in another person's User Content and does not change its ownership or confidentiality. Configuration or source needed to build and run a Modification must be supplied with secrets and User Content removed and documented placeholders or synthetic fixtures where needed; this does not permit concealing necessary Software source as data. Privacy and access control must also be implemented technically; this license does not encrypt data.

